WEBVTT

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:13.450
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.090
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.150
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.560
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.670
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.810
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.370
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.560
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.630
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.720
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.480
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:02.760
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.690
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:13.140
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.450
Takara Fansubs

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.970
<i>The "Black Brothers" alliance of chimney sweeps grew stronger,</i>

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.960
<i>...with Alfredo at its center.</i>

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:45.060
<i>Romeo did his best to follow the example set by Alfredo,</i>

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.470
<i>...who possessed such magnificent leadership skills.</i>

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.450
Episode 17:

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.450
Showdown at San Babila Church.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.900
That's right, Piccolo. It's a letter from Romeo.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.960
Look how much he's already learned to write!

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:14.550
Did you know he's been working with his Black Brothers friends?

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.470
"Dear Miss Angeletta. Here is today's report."

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:25.680
"We the Black Brothers have been working on a plan."

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.190
"Alfredo has decided to do battle with the Wolf Pack...

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.020
...this Thursday behind San Babila Church."

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:40.380
<i>Alfredo was by no means a boy fond of fighting.</i>

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.110
<i>But his comrades had been attacked many times.</i>

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:52.060
<i>The new members Baltolo and Giuliano were no exception.</i>

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.150
<i>To protect his friends,</i>

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.280
<i>...the Wolf Pack had to be confronted once and for all.</i>

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.390
<i>Alfredo was sure of it.</i>

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.720
<i>Romeo thought so, too.</i>

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.480
<i>Preparations were made between jobs.</i>

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.720
<i>It was hard work, but they pooled their strength earnestly.</i>

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.080
We'll take over, Augusto.
- Thanks.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:15.980
Finished!

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.310
Special-made soot bombs.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.780
Alfredo!

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:32.910
<i>And finally... Thursday.</i>

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.070
<i>It was the day of their confrontation with the Wolf Pack.</i>

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:39.340
Are we clear?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.110
Like I've said before,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.260
...today the Wolf Pack will waylay Michaelo right here.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.810
Michaelo will lead them into that alley.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.420
I'm scared.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:55.900
Don't worry, Michaelo.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.820
Everything will go according to plan.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.750
Right -- if you do it just like we practiced.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.540
What... what if I make a mistake?
- You'll be fine.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.850
You've practiced it so many times.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.090
Show some courage!
- We'll be right behind you, Michaelo.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.810
Let's beat the Wolf Pack!

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.570
Let's give it the best we've got, Michaelo.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.120
Come on, Wolf Pack!

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.570
Are you going out, Giovanni?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.390
Yeah. The Scorpion Gang asked me to stop by...

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.330
The Scorpion Gang!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.150
We just beat those guys to a pulp.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.510
Haven't they had enough?

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.860
It wasn't Tonio or Marco who called me.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.640
It was Claudio.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:42.410
Claudio?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:47.780
Shall I go, too?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.720
You won't be needed.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.500
He'll be fine. This is Giovanni we're talking about.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.010
More importantly, I'm hungry.
- Right!

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.170
Come to think of it, it's Thursday.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.860
Doesn't that chimney sweep, what's-his-name,

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.260
...head back home after buying food today?

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.040
That's right: Michaelo the crybaby.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.220
It's the day he takes his usual route.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.830
Go grab it, Leo.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.590
Hey, everybody.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.830
Isn't it about time we stopped picking on those guys?

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.980
Why?

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.110
I don't like picking on weak guys.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.730
Go for a tough guy if you gotta get someone.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.540
Bah! That won't stop me.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.610
Just give 'em a sound thrashing.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.700
Besides, they're outsiders.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.810
Bring back a lot.
- You don't have to tell me.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.420
I want an apple.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.270
I hope the Wolf Pack doesn't show up.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.660
There he is!

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.410
It's Leo the Louse!

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:04.800
Stupid. Think you can get away from the Wolf Pack?

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.740
What a lot of trouble you are.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.850
Ha! How do you like that, nitwit?
Now hand it over.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.430
Romeo!

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.070
What do you guys want?
- Leo the Louse!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.100
No, don't! I'm alone, you know.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.350
We're not like you fellows in the Wolf Pack.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.900
Starting now, we won't let you get away with whatever you want!

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.870
We challenge the Wolf Pack to a fight.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:52.890
Come to the back of San Babila Church this afternoon at five.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.660
San Babila Church?

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:59.920
Don't forget to give them the message.
- All right.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.870
Go on, get out of here, louse!

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.600
All right! It worked!

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.330
You did well, Michaelo.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.230
Okay, everybody, on to the next part of the plan.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.380
Right!

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.410
Those chimney sweeps said what?!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.260
That they'll be waiting for us behind San Babila Church.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.300
So they've decided to challenge the Wolf Pack. How interesting.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.850
Those upstarts.
We'll grind 'em to bits!

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.370
Like this!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.810
My fists can't wait.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:40.610
All right, then, let's accept their invitation.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.220
What'll we say to Giovanni?

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:45.620
We got more than enough right here to take on those weaklings.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.160
Yeah, that's true enough.
- Come on, let's go quickly.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.990
San Babila Church, right?

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.450
There's no one here.

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.780
Leo, is this really the right place?

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:14.230
Yes, it is. I'm sure they said behind San Babila Church.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.280
Over here.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.670
Romeo -- why you -- !

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:25.620
Now!

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.570
You punks!

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:51.920
Damn it!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:53.830
Where did you go?

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.050
Damn it!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.400
Fight fair and square!

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:24.320
You did it.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.220
You lured us into a trap, didn't you. Cowards!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.420
We did it because you're always picking on us.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.300
Let's get him!
- Stop it!

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:39.060
Sorry about that, but we never could have beaten you otherwise.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.690
And besides, I don't want to fight a girl.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.420
Alfredo!

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.290
This guy's a girl?!

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:47.880
Let her go.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:48.610
Sure.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:52.910
Don't let me out!
I didn't ask for your help!

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.650
Don't underestimate me!

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.780
I'm brave enough to not lose a fight with you boys!

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:01.970
If you want to fight, go ahead, try me!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.960
Can this really be a girl?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:07.850
Dante!

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:09.330
I'm okay.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.350
But that surprised me.
Woke me up, too.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.060
It's the first time I've ever been hit by a girl.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.230
But since you're cute, I'll let you off the hook.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:27.050
I'm worried about one thing, though.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.460
Worried about what?
- Hey!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.030
Hey! What's so funny?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.110
I...

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.340
Sorry. Forget it.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:57.030
Take care of her, Antonio.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.980
Let me out! Hey!

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.890
Think of it as payment for picking on us so long.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.700
I'll tell you who we are:

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.580
Milan's heroes, the Black Brothers!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.890
Black Brothers! Hoorah!

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:25.770
Black Brothers?

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.900
It's an alliance we put together for us chimney sweeps.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.170
Alfredo created and named it.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.640
We've won the battle of San Babila Church!

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.320
Right!

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.530
<i>Why isn't Giovanni here?</i>

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.130
Here's celebrating the Black Brothers' victory!

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.480
Yeah!

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.780
I feel so relieved.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:07.030
Hey, did you see the look on Tachioni's face?

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.800
He looked just like this:
"Da-amn i-it!"

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:18.400
Now they won't attack us for a little while, at least.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:19.660
You got it.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.290
But that Nikita really is something.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.380
What's wrong, Alfredo?

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:28.980
Something's bothering me.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.480
Bothering you?

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.260
Giovanni wasn't there.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:35.490
Giovanni?

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:44.520
We won't have silenced the Wolf Pack until we take care of Giovanni.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:50.870
But if she'd been a he I'd have trounced him good!

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:57.020
Everyone! From today on, absolutely don't do anything alone.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:58.170
Why?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.410
Those guys are not going to be so easy to deal with.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:04.670
Anyway, let's call out to each other when we're out on the streets.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:08.370
No matter what happens, don't go anyplace alone.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:09.410
Understood?

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.150
Yes... I understand.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.200
Today we're going to knock you down for sure.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.670
If you want to apologize, now's the time.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:32.680
Get him, Claudio!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.490
No one can win against Claudio.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.560
We're going to get to see your crying face.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.810
Are you ready, Giovanni?

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.630
Bastard! You'll pay for that!

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.640
Here's the stopper!

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:01.800
Claudio...

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:12.690
All right! We surrender for good this time!

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:15.380
You're the strongest guy in Milan.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.560
So you finally understand.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.650
The Scorpion Gang is finished.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.410
Please let us join the Wolf Pack.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:23.380
Me, too!

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:24.260
Me, too!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.100
Me, too!

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.010
It's just like you said.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.820
Without taking out Giovanni, we haven't beaten the Wolf Pack.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.270
They'll be back for revenge, no doubt about it.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:43.970
Be as careful as possible.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:44.520
Yeah.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.710
Don't worry. I'll be thinking up a plan tonight.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.250
Okay.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.860
See you. I'll be waiting in the usual spot tomorrow.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.340
All right. See you tomorrow.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.540
Hey!

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:08.370
Oh, it's you.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:13.570
Did you want something?

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:14.650
Listen here...!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.270
What?

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.410
What's wrong? You wanted to ask me something, didn't you?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.970
Why were you laughing back then?

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:27.480
Eh?

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.470
You looked at my face and were about to say something.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.330
Aren't you going to answer me?!

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.020
I was reminded...
...of another girl I know.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:47.760
<i>Alfredo was thinking about his younger sister, Bianca.</i>

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:53.440
<i>It's not that Nikita and Bianca resembled each other...</i>

00:15:54.130 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>...but rather, he saw a bit of Bianca in Nikita's unyielding spirit.</i>

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.670
On the outside that girl always acted strong-minded and stubborn...

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:09.070
...but she was gentle and always lonely on the inside... like you.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:16.190
I was constantly at the mercy of her pranks.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.410
I'd think, "What'll she do next?"

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.110
That's what I was thinking back then.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.450
So... have I answered your question?

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.410
What kind of an answer is that!?

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:35.980
I had hoped that from now on...

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:37.420
What!

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:41.210
Why do you dress up like a boy?

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:48.150
I thought you would look really nice if you put a flower in your hair.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.470
Who asked for your advice?!
Why would I... put a flower...!

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:04.060
I detest your sort, you with your patronizing face!

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.450
You watch: as long as you're the leader,

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.450
...I'll do all I can to defeat you Black Brothers.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:33.490
I thought you would look really nice if you put a flower in your hair.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.320
<i>I won't let a guy like...
like that beat me.</i>

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:40.370
You scum!

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:44.200
You say the Black Brothers utterly trounced you?

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.520
And you call yourselves part of the Wolf Pack?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.050
Heh. The "Black Brothers", is it?

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.760
They'll be a handy way of killing time.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:57.050
I'll make them give up this little game.

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.010
You'd better not underestimate the guy called Alfredo.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.860
He's a sharp one.

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:02.740
Alfredo?

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.660
A friend of that Romeo.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:05.430
Of Romeo?

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:06.710
That's it!

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:10.720
There's one sure way of defeating those guys.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:15.210
What way?

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.290
Through Alfredo.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:18.830
Keep going, Nikita.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:23.520
It's Alfredo who comes up with every part of their plans.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:28.310
So if Alfredo disappears, the Black Brothers will fall apart.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.190
Spatza camino!

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:54.100
Spatza caminoo...!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:01.680
But man, did we ever look cool yesterday.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.150
That was cool!
- Very!

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.750
Now we don't have to be afraid of the Wolf Pack.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:07.500
Yeah.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.520
If they show up, we'll just blast 'em with soot again.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.900
Yep. They'll be just like this.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.850
Well... I guess I'll head back to work now.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.480
Umm...

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.980
Leo the Louse!

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.140
What are you doing here?

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.670
I came to apologize.
- To apologize?

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:33.790
Yeah... because we've done only bad things up until now.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:35.860
I'm serious!

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.820
I'm asking sincerely, aren't I?

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.800
So that's it. So you guys have finally come around.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:46.400
We're not mad at you guys any more.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.460
Not since you're apologizing like this.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.650
Really?
- Yeah.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.560
We want to apologize by giving you some fruit.

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:56.140
Can one of you come pick them up?

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:59.140
Oh... I need to get back to work.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.170
I'll go, then.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:02.490
This way.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.400
But... should we do this? Alfredo said not to go anywhere alone.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:13.090
It'll be fine. You saw that Leo's face, didn't you?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.270
We won't hear a peep from the Wolf Pack.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.180
Hey!

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:18.600
Is anybody there?

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.450
Hey, Romeo!

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:23.340
Did you hear Leo's voice a second ago?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.170
He was just here.
- What?

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.950
But he left with Michaelo.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.570
With Michaelo? Why?

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:32.470
He was going to get some fruit.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.340
As a gesture of apology, he said.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:35.690
Don't tell me he went... alone?

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:36.740
He went alone.

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.190
Michaelo!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:40.870
Is it still far?

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.500
No, it's just up here.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.300
See? Here it is.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.200
Help!

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:01.890
Michaelo! Michaelo!
Where are you?

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:09.140
<i>You KNEW about staying together...</i>

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:10.510
<i>...so why did you go alone, Michaelo?</i>

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:12.160
Oh!

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:20.800
<i>A letter?</i>

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.200
"We've taken Michaelo."

00:21:31.610 --> 00:21:33.080
"We've taken Michaelo."

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:38.610
"If you want him back, hand over your leader, Alfredo -- alone."

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.040
Alfredo?

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:01.540
<i>Alfredo went alone to the Wolf Pack to get Michaelo back.</i>

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:03.940
<i>Wait for me, Alfredo!</i>

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.990
<i>I'll come there myself to rescue you.</i>

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:11.060
See you then!

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:11.060
<i>Sing our Song of Unity on into the Dawn!</i>

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:11.060
Next time:

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:17.960
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:30.670
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.770 --> 00:22:34.970
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:39.170
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:43.370
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:48.280
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.180
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:59.480
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:05.080
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.280
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
